-      "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "Reviewed 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57, 2 commits, both fork-authored: 4dd165625 'server: do not propagate kv-mean-center bias to draft model contexts (#81)' (a real correctness fix on a path we run - worth reading) and 9ca265a57 'cuda: extract Q2_0 elements via __byte_perm (#104)' (CUDA, skip, this box is Vulkan). Pin advanced. WARNING - THE SMALL NUMBER IS MISLEADING, and this is the one fork where the 'default branch understates' defect is REAL (it is not real for tq3, which is where the register previously claimed it): prisml/prism last moved 2026-07-31, while the fork has fix/metal-im2col-dispatch-wide-set-rows at 2026-08-16, feat/tq1_0-cuda at 2026-08-13, prism-v6-g128-arm-metal-fixes at 2026-08-11, and prism-v6 + prism-v6-dspark-dflash at 2026-08-10. The ENTIRE v6 line is invisible to this pin. CONTRACT FLAG D: prisml/prism-v6 moved Q2_0_G128 to type id 142 with geometry (128, 2+32) - byte-for-byte our g128 - and it IS in their gguf-py. 142 is free for us so there is no collision, but TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 5's premise 'PrismML shipped 128-value-per-block data under type-id 42' no longer describes their current line, and the g128 gate's whole rationale rests on that premise. Note prisml/prism itself has NO g128 in its enum at all (COUNT=43). The `ref` was NOT changed: prism is the true default branch and this file's _comment is emphatic about not guessing a branch, but the work is elsewhere - that is a register-semantics call for HQ, above a review lane.",
+      "pin": "7529fdaaf",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "PIN DELIBERATELY NOT ADVANCED, and this entry is the reason. I DID review 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57 (below) and briefly advanced the pin to 9ca265a57 - then reverted it, because advancing made `currency` print 'prisml ... current' while the fork's actual unreviewed work sits on branches this ref never sees. currency's table is what a reader acts on; a pin_review body is not. A green row that has to be corrected by prose is worse than a BEHIND row, and it would contradict the reasoning that keeps ciru pinned back in this same file. The BEHIND-by-2 this produces UNDERSTATES the real backlog, which is the v6 line - but BEHIND is a live signal and current is a false one. Reviewed 7529fdaaf..9ca265a57, 2 commits, both fork-authored: 4dd165625 'server: do not propagate kv-mean-center bias to draft model contexts (#81)' (a real correctness fix on a path we run - worth reading) and 9ca265a57 'cuda: extract Q2_0 elements via __byte_perm (#104)' (CUDA, skip, this box is Vulkan). Pin advanced. WARNING - THE SMALL NUMBER IS MISLEADING, and this is the one fork where the 'default branch understates' defect is REAL (it is not real for tq3, which is where the register previously claimed it): prisml/prism last moved 2026-07-31, while the fork has fix/metal-im2col-dispatch-wide-set-rows at 2026-08-16, feat/tq1_0-cuda at 2026-08-13, prism-v6-g128-arm-metal-fixes at 2026-08-11, and prism-v6 + prism-v6-dspark-dflash at 2026-08-10. The ENTIRE v6 line is invisible to this pin. CONTRACT FLAG D: prisml/prism-v6 moved Q2_0_G128 to type id 142 with geometry (128, 2+32) - byte-for-byte our g128 - and it IS in their gguf-py. 142 is free for us so there is no collision, but TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 5's premise 'PrismML shipped 128-value-per-block data under type-id 42' no longer describes their current line, and the g128 gate's whole rationale rests on that premise. Note prisml/prism itself has NO g128 in its enum at all (COUNT=43). The `ref` was NOT changed: prism is the true default branch and this file's _comment is emphatic about not guessing a branch, but the work is elsewhere - that is a register-semantics call for HQ, above a review lane.",
       "role": "ternary Q2_0 g128 lineage, f16 recurrent S-state, DSpark",
       "track_tags": false
     },
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@
       "ref": "origin/HEAD",
       "pin": "f6124e914",
       "pin_review": "lane-110C turbokv matrix (trial-evidence/110/turbokv-matrix.json) measured this tree end-to-end; WHT non-interchangeability proven against it (RESUME finding 4). That measurement was of c26cbdffc's LINEAGE - see the lane-143 key for why the sha moved and why the claim survives.",
-      "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "THE OLD PIN WAS NOT MERELY BEHIND, IT WAS ON A LINEAGE THE FORK'S HEAD NEVER TOOK. c26cbdffc is 'Merge pull request #225 from TheTom/fix-ui-assets-partial-dist' (2026-07-18). `git branch -r --contains c26cbdffc` returns exactly two refs, turboquant/fix/vulkan-turbo3-flat-dequant-241 and turboquant/tom/merge-upstream-dsv4 - it is NOT contained by feature/turboquant-kv-cache, which is what origin/HEAD resolves to. merge-base(c26cbdffc, head) = 1fd6dfe9f, an UPSTREAM UI commit from 2026-06-14, and rev-list --left-right --count gives 338/841. So any 'c26cbdffc..head = 841 commits behind' figure is divergent-history arithmetic, not a delta. Re-pinned to f6124e914 (2026-08-17). The lane-110C claim above SURVIVES the move: the TurboQuant KV/WHT surface it measured is intact at the head, so this was a stale pin, not an evaporated finding. MEASURED DELTA from the merge-base: 816 non-merge, of which 151 are fork-authored (--not upstream/master) and 33 touch turbo/TQ quant or kernels; the other ~118 are upstream sync, DeepseekV4/DSpark, UI and CI. WHAT WE TAKE, ranked. (1) 7f8302613 'ggml-cpu : declare turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size extern, not a second definition' (2026-08-07) plus follow-up c7d6442dd (2026-08-12) - THIS IS A LIVE DEFECT IN OUR TREE. recut/2026-08-16 carries the pre-fix shape: ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:26 has `GGML_API int turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size;` inside extern C with no `extern`, and ops.cpp is C++, so that is a SECOND DEFINITION in libggml-cpu while the real one lives in ggml-turbo-quant.c:31-32 in libggml-base. The fix's own message names our platform: 'ELF interposition may merge them; two-level-namespace and DLL targets will not', so on our Windows DLL build the SET_ROWS handler and the quantizer plausibly operate on DIFFERENT variables and turbo3 group-size propagation is silently link-order dependent. CHECKED in source at both refs; NOT built or run - this lane's fence forbids builds, so the runtime consequence is reasoned, not observed. A build lane should confirm and take both. (2) cd4c3a1f6 'remove the per-call mallocs from the TurboQuant vec_dot kernels' (CPU, pure win). (3) e130aef60 'close complete-audit findings - 7 port regressions + TQ4_1S dp4a kernel' (an audit of exactly the port we did). (4) The Vulkan cluster of 2026-08-03/04, our backend: 844678bf2 SET_ROWS block decomposition for turbo weight types, 160649054 TQ MUL_MAT_ID size gate limited to the f16 dequant fallback, 5f5ef77ad TQ4_1S pipeline wiring, 4f2013d66 turbo3 KV pipeline, b43efe599 turbo3 wiring correction, 353ac109e + 637300387 mul_mat_vec_id add / MUL_MAT_ID reject, b514ae496 TQ3_1S weight type, b0c39adac TQ4_1S wiring restored - our merge 70a752991 post-dates these so several are probably already in, and EACH needs a content diff before cherry-picking (per-commit tree comparison across a rebase is a build lane's job, not a register lane's). (5) f050a2501 + a70a324fa fattn-vec turbo-K split for a VGPR spill, re-gated on the LUT rather than on D - authored for HIP/CUDA, but the gating correction is architecture-general. WHAT WE SKIP AND WHY: 3243b2875 (fused TQ3_1S mul_mat on HIP gfx1100 - our rig is a 780M gfx1103 on Vulkan, not HIP), 8365224ee (CUDA-only garbage-output fix), ffc210bfb (arm64 CI), 07e01ec54 + ce3dce77b + aab782c1b (DeepseekV4/DSpark model support - a different slot), and the ~118 upstream-sync commits which arrive with the next upstream move. CONTRACT CHECK: CLEAN. This head defines TQ3_1S=45 and TQ4_1S=46, exactly the ids TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 3.1 reserves, so verbatim adoption still holds. Runtime types sit at 43/44/47. FLAG E, the one silent-capable collision in the whole contract, CONFIRMED AT THIS HEAD: TURBO2_0 is id 43 and our Q2_0_G128 is id 43, and block_turbo2_0 (ggml_half + qs[128/4] = 34 B / 128 values) is BYTE-IDENTICAL AND FIELD-IDENTICAL to block_q2_0_g128, so gguf_init's row-size check has nothing to separate them and the g128 metadata gate keys off a marker a turbo2 file would never carry - a serialized TURBO2_0 read as our g128 would dequantize wrongly and KEEP GOING (turbo2 is WHT-rotated Lloyd-Max, ours is plain scaled). NOT TRIGGERED today, verified three ways at this head: no LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_TURBO2_0, no TURBO target in tools/quantize/quantize.cpp, no TURBO entry in gguf-py. Also, block_turbo2_0's in-source comment still reads '// 10 bytes total' while its static_assert computes 34 - contract section 1.1 warned about exactly those stale comments and it is still stale here. REGISTER DEFECT FLAGGED TO HQ, NOT FIXED HERE: this fork is registered TWICE - as this local_checkouts entry and as the `turboquant` git remote of the engine repo - and the two disagree. The sibling clone src/llama-cpp-turboquant is at a33ef00b1 (2026-06-23) with origin/feature/turboquant-kv-cache at fca3093c9, both OLDER than the remote head this pin now names. One of the two should be authoritative. Full review: research/local-inference/2026-08-17-fork-delta-review.md",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "THE OLD PIN WAS NOT MERELY BEHIND, IT WAS ON A LINEAGE THE FORK'S HEAD NEVER TOOK. c26cbdffc is 'Merge pull request #225 from TheTom/fix-ui-assets-partial-dist' (2026-07-18). `git branch -r --contains c26cbdffc` returns exactly two refs, turboquant/fix/vulkan-turbo3-flat-dequant-241 and turboquant/tom/merge-upstream-dsv4 - it is NOT contained by feature/turboquant-kv-cache, which is what origin/HEAD resolves to. merge-base(c26cbdffc, head) = 1fd6dfe9f, an UPSTREAM UI commit from 2026-06-14, and rev-list --left-right --count gives 338/841. So any 'c26cbdffc..head = 841 commits behind' figure is divergent-history arithmetic, not a delta. Re-pinned to f6124e914 (2026-08-17). The lane-110C claim above SURVIVES the move: the TurboQuant KV/WHT surface it measured is intact at the head, so this was a stale pin, not an evaporated finding. MEASURED DELTA from the merge-base: 816 non-merge, of which 151 are fork-authored (--not upstream/master) and 33 touch turbo/TQ quant or kernels; the other ~118 are upstream sync, DeepseekV4/DSpark, UI and CI. WHAT WE TAKE, ranked. (1) 7f8302613 'ggml-cpu : declare turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size extern, not a second definition' (2026-08-07) plus follow-up c7d6442dd (2026-08-12) - NO-OP FOR US, take only for tidiness. SELF-REFUTATION, recorded because this lane first wrote the opposite and the correction is the valuable part: I initially read recut's ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:26 `GGML_API int turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size;` as a SECOND DEFINITION in libggml-cpu against the real one in ggml-turbo-quant.c:31-32, and called it a live defect on our Windows DLL build on the strength of the fix's own commit message ('ELF interposition may merge them; two-level-namespace and DLL targets will not'). THAT WAS WRONG, and the error was not expanding the macro. In recut/2026-08-16:ggml/include/ggml.h, GGML_API expands to `... extern` in ALL FOUR branches (dllexport extern / dllimport extern / visibility-default extern / bare extern), so ops.cpp:26 is a DECLARATION on every platform and every build mode, and no second definition exists anywhere in our tree. Worse for the original framing: at turboquant's own pre-fix commit 7f8302613^ only the NON-Windows branch lacked `extern` (`__attribute__((visibility(\"default\")))` with no extern), so their bug lived on ELF/macOS and their commit message has the platform exactly BACKWARDS - the Windows branches already carried extern. Our tree is correct as it stands; these two commits change nothing for us. (2) cd4c3a1f6 'remove the per-call mallocs from the TurboQuant vec_dot kernels' (CPU, pure win). (3) e130aef60 'close complete-audit findings - 7 port regressions + TQ4_1S dp4a kernel' (an audit of exactly the port we did). (4) The Vulkan cluster of 2026-08-03/04, our backend: 844678bf2 SET_ROWS block decomposition for turbo weight types, 160649054 TQ MUL_MAT_ID size gate limited to the f16 dequant fallback, 5f5ef77ad TQ4_1S pipeline wiring, 4f2013d66 turbo3 KV pipeline, b43efe599 turbo3 wiring correction, 353ac109e + 637300387 mul_mat_vec_id add / MUL_MAT_ID reject, b514ae496 TQ3_1S weight type, b0c39adac TQ4_1S wiring restored - our merge 70a752991 post-dates these so several are probably already in, and EACH needs a content diff before cherry-picking (per-commit tree comparison across a rebase is a build lane's job, not a register lane's). (5) f050a2501 + a70a324fa fattn-vec turbo-K split for a VGPR spill, re-gated on the LUT rather than on D - authored for HIP/CUDA, but the gating correction is architecture-general. WHAT WE SKIP AND WHY: 3243b2875 (fused TQ3_1S mul_mat on HIP gfx1100 - our rig is a 780M gfx1103 on Vulkan, not HIP), 8365224ee (CUDA-only garbage-output fix), ffc210bfb (arm64 CI), 07e01ec54 + ce3dce77b + aab782c1b (DeepseekV4/DSpark model support - a different slot), and the ~118 upstream-sync commits which arrive with the next upstream move. CONTRACT CHECK: CLEAN. This head defines TQ3_1S=45 and TQ4_1S=46, exactly the ids TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 3.1 reserves, so verbatim adoption still holds. Runtime types sit at 43/44/47. FLAG E, the one silent-capable collision in the whole contract, CONFIRMED AT THIS HEAD: TURBO2_0 is id 43 and our Q2_0_G128 is id 43, and block_turbo2_0 (ggml_half + qs[128/4] = 34 B / 128 values) is BYTE-IDENTICAL AND FIELD-IDENTICAL to block_q2_0_g128, so gguf_init's row-size check has nothing to separate them and the g128 metadata gate keys off a marker a turbo2 file would never carry - a serialized TURBO2_0 read as our g128 would dequantize wrongly and KEEP GOING (turbo2 is WHT-rotated Lloyd-Max, ours is plain scaled). THAT 'SILENT' VERDICT IS CODE-DERIVED, NOT CONTRACT-PROSE: read at recut/2026-08-16:src/llama-model-loader.cpp, llama_gguf_q2_0_g128_gate returns FALSE on `key < 0` (line 133-135) without throwing, and the only consumer is `if (q2_0_g128_enabled)` at :870 which skips the span check and llama_remap_q2_0_g128 entirely. Nothing on the false branch rejects id-43 tensors. gguf_init has already validated their spans against ggml_row_size(43) = 34 B / 128, which a turbo2_0 file matches exactly. So the file parses clean and our plain-scaled g128 kernel runs on rotated data. NOT TRIGGERED today, verified three ways at this head: no LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_TURBO2_0, no TURBO target in tools/quantize/quantize.cpp, no TURBO entry in gguf-py. Also, block_turbo2_0's in-source comment still reads '// 10 bytes total' while its static_assert computes 34 - contract section 1.1 warned about exactly those stale comments and it is still stale here. REGISTER DEFECT FLAGGED TO HQ, NOT FIXED HERE: this fork is registered TWICE - as this local_checkouts entry and as the `turboquant` git remote of the engine repo - and the two disagree. The sibling clone src/llama-cpp-turboquant is at a33ef00b1 (2026-06-23) with origin/feature/turboquant-kv-cache at fca3093c9, both OLDER than the remote head this pin now names. One of the two should be authoritative. Full review: research/local-inference/2026-08-17-fork-delta-review.md",
